1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,100
What if everyone turned 6... for 5 seconds?

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,030
Times Square. Rush hour.

3
00:00:05,305 --> 00:00:08,280
The average American adult? 5′6″.

4
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:10,930
Second 1. Everyone drops 20 inches,

5
00:00:11,025 --> 00:00:12,775
and three quarters of their weight.

6
00:00:13,079 --> 00:00:16,109
Shoes slip off. Grip strength? Down 80%.

7
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:20,670
Second 2. Every seat belt now crosses a 6-year-old's neck.

8
00:00:20,906 --> 00:00:23,496
Adult belts fit at 4′9″ and up.

9
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:27,130
Second 3. Nobody can reach the brake.

10
00:00:27,435 --> 00:00:31,865
At 25 mph, that's 37 feet... every second.

11
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:35,330
Second 4. Most new cars... brake themselves.

12
00:00:35,677 --> 00:00:37,647
Automatic emergency braking.

13
00:00:37,970 --> 00:00:40,020
The old taxi? Not so much.

14
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:41,310
Second 5.

15
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:44,990
Its airbag fires... at a 6-year-old.

16
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:47,870
And... everyone's back.

17
00:00:48,115 --> 00:00:49,565
Barefoot. Pants down.

18
00:00:49,806 --> 00:00:55,096
Their heads barely shrank. By 6, the brain is about 90% adult size.

19
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:59,510
Who was in more danger: the kids walking... or the kids driving?
